1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,627
First Aid.
急救。

2
00:00:02,627 --> 00:00:36,587
A boy fell ill. His organs were damaged by the radiation of an infrared ray stove. But before the ambulance arrived, a number of other injuries happened to this unlucky boy over and over again.
一个男孩生病了。他的器官受到一台红外线炉辐射的损伤。但在救护车到达之前，这个倒霉的男孩又遭受了其他伤害，一次又一次。

3
00:00:36,587 --> 00:01:05,380
First, he was choked by some poisonous liquid from the kettle on the cupboard. Then his wrist skin was burnt by electric shock. Finally, his ankle was cut by a pan.
首先，橱柜上水壶里的有毒液体呛到了他。接着，他手腕的皮肤被电击灼伤。最后，他的脚踝被锅划破。

4
00:01:05,380 --> 00:02:11,740
Fortunately, the boy’s nurse gave him proper temporary treatments according to his complex symptoms. She mildly squeezed the poisonous liquid out of his throat and put bandages firmly in place to apply pressure to the ankle wound to stop bleeding. As for the burn, she used scissors to remove his sleeve, poured a basin of cold water over the burn to cool it and put her hands on a damp blouse to cover his swollen tissue tightly.
幸运的是，故事中的护士根据复杂症状给他做了临时处理。她轻轻地把有毒液体从他的喉部挤了出来，并将绷带牢牢固定好，给脚踝伤口加压，以止住流血。至于烧伤，她用剪刀剪去他的袖子，把一盆冷水倒在烧伤处使其降温，然后找到一件潮湿的女式衬衫，紧紧裹住他肿胀的组织。

5
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:48,300
She also inspired his bravery to fight against the unbearable pain. Her first aid made a vital difference in saving his life. A ceremony was held to honour the nurse who overcame a variety of barriers to save the boy.
她还鼓励他勇敢地忍受难以承受的疼痛。她的急救对挽救他的生命起了重要作用。人们举行仪式，表彰这位护士，她克服种种障碍，救助了这个男孩。
